 10	 * enabled agents an OpenAI-compatible gateway consumer may address as chat backends.
 11	 *
 12	 * GET /api/router/openai-agent-discovery returns one row per enabled route that
 13	 * resolves to a manifest AND has an active host port. The response is built from
 14	 * `route.hostPath` (via the exported readEnabledAgentManifest) plus the
 15	 * enabled-agent fallback — never a `route.manifestPath`. It deliberately emits NO
 16	 * `http://127.0.0.1:<routerPort>` base URLs: the consumer composes the actual
 17	 * call URL from its own PLOINKY_ROUTER_URL, the returned `routerPath`, and
 18	 * `chatCompletionsPath`. The container-internal port stays inside the router.
 19	 *
 20	 * The endpoint is for agents, not browsers: it requires an HTTP Agent Assertion
 21	 * (`Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`) bound to this exact request surface, with `rch`
 22	 * computed via computeRchHttp() (not computeRchTool()). It is dispatched BEFORE the
 23	 * generic session-auth gate in RoutingServer, like /policy/command, so a browser
 24	 * session is neither sufficient nor required.
